On 05/02/2018 03:36 AM, zrc2...@gmail.com wrote:
> I am responding to an old post here but I am also interested in tackling
> a manova-type question using SEM. I have not been successful in finding
> possible updates you mentioned and was curious (1) if there might have
> been any updates

Sadly, no. As often happens, the student I mentioned in the old post
left academia, and that work was never finished. It is still on my
'things-I-should-work-on' list, so perhaps one day I may pick this up again.

(2) you might have suggestions for addressing these
> questions in Lavaan.

It is easy to use lavaan to run a 'MANOVA' like analysis. And it works
wonderful if you have a large sample. But for small samples, the classic
(large-sample-based) tests are just not good enough. I think the best
option for the moment (using lavaan) is to use bootstrapping.

Yves.

